This repository contains the raw data used for the retrospective validation of a Large Language Model (LLM)-hybrid screening process. The data is organized into three distinct phases corresponding to the systematic review pipeline:  
Phase 1: Title and Abstract Screening (k= 10% of 1704) -> 170 trials
Phase 2: Full-text Screening (k= 10% of 335) -> 34 trials  
Phase 3: Final Inclusion (k=38) -> 38 trials 

Structure and "Record Number" Logic
The files provided are EndNote exports containing the specific study pools for each phase.
Sorting Requirement: To replicate the study selection, the reader must sort the libraries by "Record Number" in EndNote.  
ID Translation: The EndNote ID numbers used in the validation protocol (e.g., ID 5727) are based on the total cumulative sources imported into the primary investigator's EndNote application.  
External Reproduction: If a reader imports these individual phase files into a new EndNote library, the record numbers will likely be reset (e.g., ID 5727 may become ID 1). 
To compare specific results, the reader must "translate" the numbers based on the sorted order, assuming EndNote maintains record number consistency across the import/export of these specific subsets.  
Keep in mind: For all duplicate references, the original is not included, to keep the randomization process unbiased. Covidence was used to find the originally assessed trial. 

Files included in this repository are as follows:
  1) "LLM Validation.pdf" -> The raw LLM Validation protocol and matrix-dataset with notes
  2) "LLM Title and Abstract.enl" -> All randomly chosen references used from the Title and Abstract screening 
  3) "LLM Full-text.enl" ->  All randomly chosen references used from the Full-text screening
  4) "LLM Included trials.enl" ->  References for all included trials

